 ## Overview
-This family defines the iterative optimization procedure that minimizes a photometric or physical loss between rendered images and ground-truth observations by updating the parameters of a scene representation (e.g., neural radiance fields, meshes, or transfer functions) [S1, unofficial]. It solves the inverse rendering problem by differentiating the volume rendering equation with respect to scene parameters, enabling gradient-based learning of geometry and appearance [NeRF Training Loop](970-nerf-training-loop.md). It sets itself apart from [NeRF Evaluation and Metric Calculation](3079-nerf-evaluation-and-metric-calculation.md) by using stochastic ray sampling and adaptive integration strategies to facilitate gradient propagation, rather than deterministic rendering for metric assessment.
