-Differentiation strategies fall into three main categories [NeRF Training Loop](970-nerf-training-loop.md):
-1. **Reverse-Mode Automatic Differentiation (AD):** Standard backpropagation through the computational graph. This requires storing $O(kn)$ intermediate states (where $n$ is pixels and $k$ is samples), leading to high memory usage [NeRF Training Loop](970-nerf-training-loop.md).
