 ### Rip-NeRF Optimization
-Optimization process for Rip-NeRF involving tiny MLP weights and ripmaps $R$. Learning rate is scaled by 10x for $R$ due to its direct scene representation role, with a base learning rate of $2 \times 10^{-3}$ reduced by 0.6x at steps 60K, 90K, 100K, and 108K over 120K iterations. Batch size is dynamically adjusted to maintain ~256K spheres per batch. MLP weights are initialized via Glorot and Bengio (2010), and ripmaps $R$ via uniform distribution over $[-0.01, 0.01]$. Optimizer is AdamW [S2].
